  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting your walls to look like new after storm damage takes a bit of finesse, especially when it comes to painting and finishing. You want that seamless look, right? The process generally starts after all the drying and drywall repair is done. First, you'll need to prime the repaired area. This is super important because it helps seal the new material and provides a uniform base. Next, apply joint compound as needed to blend any patched areas smoothly into the existing wall. Once that's dry, a good sanding is key to make sure everything is perfectly smooth. Then, you'll prime again, and finally, it's time for the paint. For the best results, you might need to repaint a broader section, or even the whole wall, to ensure a uniform appearance, especially if you're matching textures or colors. Don't forget about matching the sheen too – a slight difference can make repairs stand out. If you're tackling extensive patching or challenging texture matching, bringing in a pro from HH Remodeling LLC can make all the difference in achieving that flawless finish."
    }
  ],
